{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529476-v5-homebrew-telyavalic-tremere-loresheet","id":1529476,"title":"(V5 Homebrew) Telyavalic Tremere loresheet","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-25T17:26:41-08:00","id":1529476,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon11.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> (V5 Homebrew) Telyavalic Tremere loresheet","content":"After poking through Blood Sigils a little bit, I got some ideas for this which I thought I'd jot down. Like other loresheets, this one's a combination of various sources drawing inspiration from each to blend to a single whole, not necessarily linked to a bloodline but more a social sect that's formed in the wake of the V5 metaplot events.<br /> <br /> <b>Legacy of the Shepards (Tremere only)</b><br /> <br /> Following the fall of Vienna, grimoires and texts long thought forgotten or destroyed containing Tremere clan's oldest and dirtiest secrets were recovered, copied, and shared among those of Houses Carna and Ipsissimus. The truth of the Tremere's betrayal and destruction of the Telyavelic Tremere and House Diedne under false pretense came to light, as well as some of those faction's magical secrets. Those who studied those texts realized separation and independence from the Pyramid would never be enough -- so long as it existed in any form, the Pyramid would remain a threat. For now, those who would see the Pyramid obliterated in its entirety to make way for a new generation of independent Tremere study the new possibilities offered by recovered knowledge, and wait for the opportunity to strike.<br /> <br /> <i>(Due to time constraints, I'm posting crunch now. Fluff later.)</i><br /> <br /> \u2022 <b>Sielanic Thaumaturgy: </b>If you already posses Blood Sorcery, replace one of your first-level powers with Sielanic Thaumaturgy. If you do not and later purchase your first dot of Blood Sorcery, you must select Sielanic Thaumaturgy as your first-level power. Sielanic Thaumaturgy is identical to Koldunic Sorcery as depicted in <i>Blood Sigils</i>, and counts as Koldunic Sorcery for meeting later power and ritual prerequisites.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 <b>Whispers of the Siela: </b>Gain a single dot in Haven. Regardless of any other factor including your Haven's location, design, or base rating, you may freely purchase dots in Library, Luxury, Postern, Security System, or Warding. Dots in these Haven merits do not represent physical objects or possessions but rather the aid of local spirits, and as such cannot be vandalized, destroyed, or stolen absent supernatural means. You may not select the Haunted flaw for your Haven.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Sacrifical Rituals:</b> You may substitute one Hunger's worth of animal or human sacrifice for each Rouse check made to activate Blood Sorcery rituals; sacrificing animals or humans in this way inflicts Aggravated as if you had fed harmfully. Alternatively, if you possess Sielanic Thaumaturgy you may ritualistically inflict Aggravated damage on a mortal instead of yourself at a one-for-one basis to activate the power (killing the mortal always counts as having inflicted five Aggravated). If you would incur Stains in the process of making a ritual sacrifice to fuel Blood Sorcery, add an additional Stain.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>World's Blood: </b>You may purchase dots in the discipline of Protean without tasting the blood of a vampire who possesses it, or needing to feed on animal Resonance (it still costs the same amount of experience). In addition, when you use Earth Meld you may instead merge with a living tree no smaller than your own size. When you learn Shapechange or Metamorphosis (if you do not already know either), you no longer choose default forms but instead may shift form to any animal blood bound to you, or that lives natively in your domain (forms must still obey Shapechange's restrictions to body mass).<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 <b>Justice for </b><b>the Lost: </b>You incur no Stains for any action taken in the pursuit of killing any Tremere of Houses Tremere or Goratrix, or any character allied with or in service to those Houses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-27T10:23:02-08:00","id":1529555,"title":"","content":"This does seem to me like a characterful and interesting Lore Sheet, with enough focus on both variety and expressing and portraying the possible abilities and the symbolism and themes of Telyavalic Tremere. It is also nice to see another Tremere faction given focus and portrayal in V5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1529476-v5-homebrew-telyavalic-tremere-loresheet#post1529476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Legacy of the Shepards (Tremere only)</b><br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 <b>Whispers of the Siela: </b>Gain a single dot in Haven. Regardless of any other factor including your Haven's location, design, or base rating, you may freely purchase dots in Library, Luxury, Postern, Security System, or Warding. Dots in these Haven merits do not represent physical objects or possessions but rather the aid of local spirits, and as such cannot be vandalized, destroyed, or stolen absent supernatural means. You may not select the Haunted flaw for your Haven.</div> </div> </div> </div>I especially like this because of the considerable variety of areas where Spirits ( or Magical Beings ) can aid and support the Telyavalic Tremere. Being able to purchase dots without limits in these areas and resources is certainly an impressive and appropriate portrayal of the aid of Spirits ( or Magical Beings ) . In many WoD books certainly it is detailed that they have a great variety of powers, wisdom, and actions, that also come from and express their natures and personalities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}